      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">When AtlantiCare nurse Klisa Hargrove-Loper, DNP, CRNA, APN lost her mother to breast cancer in the middle of the pandemic, she channeled her pain and loss, and turned it into something truly inspiring by founding a nonprofit organization in her mom’s memory. Watch and listen how Klisa continues her mom’s spirit of giving through her innovative foundation, seeking to bring comfort and healing to breast cancer patients.</span></span></p>\n",
